      "cve_link": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-77234",
      "cve_desc": "Improper input validation in FreeRTOS-Kernel before 11.3.1 might allow an unprivileged task on MPU-enabled ports to execute code in privileged kernel context. To remediate this issue, users should upgrade to version\u00a011.3.1 or later.",
      "exclude_reason": "A timer command submitted by an unprivileged task is executed by the timer service task as a caller-supplied function call. Affects only MPU-enabled ports (GHSA-w3vr-pr75-5hc6). ESP-IDF ships the xtensa, riscv and linux ports only, none of which set portUSING_MPU_WRAPPERS, so the MPU wrappers and the privilege boundary they enforce are not built. Same reasoning as CVE-2024-28115, already excluded in the FreeRTOS-Kernel manifest.",
      "status": "Analyzed",
      "kev_added": "",
      "kev_name": ""
    },
