      "cve_desc": "Missing queue-set type validation in xQueueAddToSet() in the FreeRTOS-Kernel before 11.3.1 might allow an unprivileged task on MPU-enabled ports with configUSE_QUEUE_SETS=1 to read privileged kernel memory.\u00a0To remediate this issue, users should upgrade to version\u00a011.3.1 or later.",
      "exclude_reason": "Missing queue-set type validation in xQueueAddToSet() leading to an out-of-bounds read in privileged kernel context. Affects only MPU-enabled ports with configUSE_QUEUE_SETS=1 (GHSA-9wvc-hqvx-5wf5). ESP-IDF ships the xtensa, riscv and linux ports only, none of which set portUSING_MPU_WRAPPERS, so there is no privileged/unprivileged split for the over-read to cross.",
